      "text": "124451.\n</think>\n<answer>143,088</answer> <|User|>The problem is asking for the product of 882 and 164, not 178 and 408. Please solve the correct problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 882 and 164? Please reason step by step.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c><think>\nTo solve the problem of finding the product of 882 and 164, we can use the standard algorithm for multiplication. Here are the steps:\n\n1. **Multiply 882 by 4 (the units digit of 164):**\n   - \\(8 \\times 4 = 32\\)\n   - Write down 2 and carry over 3.\n   - \\(8 \\times 6 = 48\\), plus the carried over 3 is 51.\n   - Write down 1 and carry over 5.\n   - \\(8 \\times 1 = 8\\), plus the carried over 5 is 13.\n   - So, \\(882 \\times 4 = 3528\\).\n\n2. **Multiply 882 by 60 (the tens digit of 164, shifted one place to the left):**\n   - \\(8 \\times 6 = 48\\)\n   - Write down 8 and carry over 4.\n   - \\(8 \\times 8 = 64\\), plus the carried over 4 is 68.\n   - Write down 8 and carry over 6.\n   - \\(8 \\times 1 = 8\\), plus the carried over 6 is 14.\n   - So, \\(882 \\times 60 = 53,040\\).\n\n3. **Multiply 882 by 100 (the hundreds digit of 164, shifted two places to the left):**\n   - \\(8 \\times 1 = 8\\)\n   - \\(8 \\times 6 = 48\\)\n   - \\(8 \\times 1 = 8\\)\n   - So, \\(882 \\times 100 = 88,200\\).\n\n4. **Add all the results together:**\n   - \\(3528\\)\n   - \\(53,040\\)\n   - \\(88,200\\)\n\n   Adding these step-by-step:\n   - \\(3528 + 53,040 = 56,568\\)\n   - \\(56,568 + 88,200 = 143,768\\)\n\nTherefore, the product of 882 and 164 is \\(143,768\\).\n\n</think>\n<answer>143,768</answer>",
